{templateType Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Styleguide\OverviewDefaultTemplate}

{*
 * The primary navigation, drawn with invented entries so that the specimen is
 * the same whichever modules this build is made of. Whether it reads as a row
 * or as a column is the theme's to decide - switch it above and watch.
 *
 * The second specimen is the case a submenu breaks, and it has to stay that
 * case: an entry that leads somewhere of its own and holds entries two levels
 * deep (tests/Template/StyleguideShowsANestedNavigationTest). One branch goes a
 * level further, which is where the two themes part - ledger draws it, atrium
 * stops at two.
 *
 * The third has the page being read two levels under an entry: ledger unfolds
 * the way to it as the page arrives, atrium only marks it. It is drawn in a
 * snippet with a way to redraw it, because the way to the page has to be
 * unfolded again in whatever Naja brings back (tests/e2e/nav-fold.spec.ts).
 *
 * The fourth is the whole navigation folded behind its Menu button, which a
 * page does only in ledger on a narrow window. Here it is folded at any width
 * and in both themes, by setting on the specimen the two tokens a theme sets
 * - the fold is those two tokens and nothing else.
 *}

{import '../../templates/furniture.latte'}
{import '../../../components/nav.latte'}

{block sgPage}
    <p class="l-measure">
        An entry with entries under it keeps its own link, and a button beside it opens what is under
        it. Ledger unfolds the entries in place, inside their entry, as deep as they go. Atrium opens
        them as a block over the page, two levels deep, where the pointer rests on the entry - and
        just as well from the button, by keyboard or by touch. The block goes away when the mouse
        leaves it, on Escape, on a click outside it, and when the focus leaves it.
    </p>

    <p class="l-measure">
        The entries the page being read is under are marked. Ledger unfolds them as the page
        arrives; atrium leaves them folded, because unfolding there covers the page. On a narrow
        window ledger folds the whole navigation behind a Menu button and opens it as a column;
        without the script it is never folded.
    </p>

    {embed block sgSection, component: $components['c-nav']}
        {block sgSectionBody}
            {specimen 'default'}
                {include nav, items: $sampleNavigation, label: 'Specimen'}
            {/specimen}

            {specimen 'with entries nested under an entry'}
                {include nav, items: $sampleNestedNavigation, label: 'Specimen with entries under an entry', testId: 'sample-subnav'}
            {/specimen}

            {specimen 'with the current page under an entry'}
                <div class="l-stack">
                    <div n:snippet="redrawnSpecimen" data-testid="sg-nav-snippet">
                        {include nav, items: $sampleCurrentNavigation, label: 'Specimen with the current page under an entry', testId: 'sample-current'}
                    </div>

                    <div class="l-cluster">
                        <a
                            n:href="redrawSpecimen!"
                            class="c-button c-button--quiet ajax"
                            data-testid="sg-nav-redraw"
                        >Draw it again</a>
                    </div>
                </div>
            {/specimen}

            {specimen 'folded behind a menu button'}
                <div style="--layout-nav-menu-toggle: inline-flex; --layout-nav-menu-folded: none">
                    {include nav, items: $sampleFoldedNavigation, label: 'Specimen folded behind a menu button', testId: 'sample-folded'}
                </div>
            {/specimen}
        {/block}
    {/embed}
{/block}
